    <pageTitle>
      <Value><![CDATA[Material Sampling Load Simulators Concrete Field Testing]]></Value>
    </pageTitle>
    <serviceCategories>
      <Value><![CDATA[[
  {
    "key": "0cddf577-7add-4192-848c-8e76f86b88d4",
    "name": "Item 1",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "01",
    "categoryHeading1": "Cored Specimens ",
    "categoryHeading2": "Specimens ",
    "category": "<p>The method is used to extract field specimens (cores) of site stabilized material for laboratory testing.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/aae7fa010b5e49bdaf79000e85b3cbe6"
  },
  {
    "key": "52cd20c8-fdee-4fec-810b-3d50fef47505",
    "name": "Item 2",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "02",
    "categoryHeading1": "Nuclear Density ",
    "categoryHeading2": "Density ",
    "category": "<p>This indirect testing method can determine the in-situ density of soil, gravel and sand material at a specific layer up to a depth of 300mm. A backscatter method is used to determine the moisture content of a surface layer.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/3271fb9b5d594743bf891ae4fe00de4e"
  },
  {
    "key": "930cfd2e-bf39-4720-9e80-bca9f04ddb23",
    "name": "Item 3",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "03",
    "categoryHeading1": "Sand Replacement",
    "categoryHeading2": "Replacement",
    "category": "<p>The sand replacement method is used to determine the in-situ density of a layer without a nuclear density gauge, and is used in situations where the nuclear density method is unsuitable.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/5541eeabf70d4996bbac8f1a2bcd90dc"
  },
  {
    "key": "6a648241-8e95-4d33-828e-60e5b3736f1d",
    "name": "Item 4",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "04",
    "categoryHeading1": " Dynamic Cone Penetrometer (DCP) ",
    "categoryHeading2": "Penetrometer (DCP) ",
    "category": "<p>This method establishes a rate of penetration into natural or compacted material. This penetration rate can be used to determine the resistance of the material as well as to interpolate a California Bearing Ratio.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/ed87753af75940fe80be9e97bc55c71e"
  },
  {
    "key": "b02764b8-197c-4340-921b-87fec52432b4",
    "name": "Item 5",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "05",
    "categoryHeading1": "Plate Load Test",
    "categoryHeading2": "Test",
    "category": "<p>This is a field test performed to determine the ultimate bearing capacity of soil and the probable settlement under a given load. The plate is placed at the desired depth, then the load is applied gradually and the settlement for each increment of load is recorded.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/2c52f14177ca469ca98f2ff5099b4b6e"
  },
  {
    "key": "da4d6bff-14e1-46a8-9f08-9b9e30c95e45",
    "name": "Item 6",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "06",
    "categoryHeading1": "Asphalt and Concrete Coring",
    "categoryHeading2": "Concrete Coring",
    "category": "<p>This method is used to extract field specimens (cores) of asphalt or concrete for laboratory testing.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/b0d3efcb42144642a9b810b29a55112a"
  },
  {
    "key": "3a40e5f5-2c93-4798-97f2-0a483a57098f",
    "name": "Item 7",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "07",
    "categoryHeading1": "Sand Patch ",
    "categoryHeading2": "Patch ",
    "category": "<p>This method is used to extract field specimens (cores) of asphalt or concrete for laboratory testing.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/547010c77a994252bba168b78e746650"
  },
  {
    "key": "e501bd6c-a13a-4e42-9492-c57053afb99f",
    "name": "Item 8",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "08",
    "categoryHeading1": "Ball Penetration Test",
    "categoryHeading2": "Test",
    "category": "<p>This method describes the penetration resistance of a road surface, the results can be used when designing a stabilized road surface.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/ac7aba25a7654da78dfab83c46670760"
  },
  {
    "key": "8cc8c781-f0e0-4fe9-90f3-38c24c259ecc",
    "name": "Item 9",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "09",
    "categoryHeading1": "Clegg Impact Hammer Testing",
    "categoryHeading2": "Testing",
    "category": "<p>The Clegg Impact Soil Tester provides a means for measuring and controlling soil strength and consolidation levels during trench re-instatement. It is also used to confirm uniform compaction over wide areas of ground, identifying poorly compacted areas and ineffective rolling of materials.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/25c08ce5bfcb4c29a49acebe064668ef"
  },
  {
    "key": "98caa91d-2147-4e2a-bd88-2ffad1908b84",
    "name": "Item 10",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "10",
    "categoryHeading1": "Rolling Straight Edge",
    "categoryHeading2": "Straight Edge",
    "category": "<p>This method is used to determine the rideability of a specific road surface area.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/e055c4319abc4285bc6c4bd12d57e81e"
  },
  {
    "key": "8ded6a41-c31a-4ac0-86a2-2bea03f7f957",
    "name": "Item 11",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "11",
    "categoryHeading1": "Sampling of Materials",
    "categoryHeading2": "Materials",
    "category": "<p>Sampling of different material used during the construction such as asphalt, soils, gravels, concrete and bitumen to obtain a sample that is representative of the material used during construction phases.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/5cdd14bc58454e5c8912bf3615854ce0"
  },
  {
    "key": "3840d374-1aaf-445e-a4e9-06940582d909",
    "name": "Item 12",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "12",
    "categoryHeading1": "Dynamic Probe Super Heavy (DPSH)",
    "categoryHeading2": "Super Heavy (DPSH)",
    "category": "<p>DPSH Testing (Dynamic Probe Super Heavy) - This method consists of driving a sacrificial or fixed cone through soil to a depth of up to 20 meters, to determine expected bearing capacity of soils. The constant energy for this heavy weight dynamic cone penetrometer is a 63.5kg weight that is raised to a height 760mm and then dropped, driving the cone into the soil or other material being tested.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/87a04ba999934633adbb8aabc6798ce1"
  },
  {
    "key": "12eded25-7ece-4b53-ae23-e859f4e7cc9f",
    "name": "Item 13",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "13",
    "categoryHeading1": "Falling Weight Deflectometer (FWD)",
    "categoryHeading2": "Deflectometer (FWD)",
    "category": "<p>The Falling Weight Deflectometer (FWD) is currently the most practical system for accurately measuring a pavement’s deflection response when it is subject to a dynamic load. This is non-destructive testing technique.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/79ea8ad6292b45c8b751826e9387034f"
  },
  {
    "key": "1c367ad4-5b4c-4f6e-ba05-62da35be8e1f",
    "name": "Item 14",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "14",
    "categoryHeading1": "International Roughness Index (IRI)",
    "categoryHeading2": "Index (IRI)",
    "category": "<p>Pave® Prof V2.0 is a modular system that uses 3D laser sensors to measure pavement profiles for applications such as highways and runways. It measures surface roughness, texture and rutting. It is capable of real-time continuous measurements of longitudinal and transverse profiles, rut depth and macro texture. These values can be used to calculate ride comfort, surface friction and surface noise generation to international standards.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/01c266abe4b546e587c268f649d69b4d"
  },
  {
    "key": "980a60c1-cc3b-4a9b-97db-bd31b57c96b2",
    "name": "Item 15",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "15",
    "categoryHeading1": "Walking profilometer  ",
    "categoryHeading2": "profilometer  ",
    "category": "<p>Smaller scale application to measure surface roughness, texture and transition irregularities, and surface rutting.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/5dcb987e1ba54a9b9f397c467ae55f9d"
  },
  {
    "key": "7d6e0991-c517-4637-8a4e-81cae156c297",
    "name": "Item 16",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "16",
    "categoryHeading1": "Model Mobile Load Simulator (MMLS 3)",
    "categoryHeading2": "Load Simulator (MMLS 3)",
    "category": "<p>An accelerated pavement testing tool applying realistic rolling wheel contact stress, to simulate traffic, moisture and temperature on the pavement layer that results in surface rutting.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/3fe34daddbd140189bd4ed5814c6480d"
  },
  {
    "key": "4aa60779-e228-4af0-9b89-adcd8dd0ea9c",
    "name": "Item 17",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "17",
    "categoryHeading1": "Concrete crack width meter/camera",
    "categoryHeading2": "meter/camera",
    "category": "<p>Investigate cracks width on concrete structures such as walls, tunnels, bridges etc. with photographic recording - accuracy of 0.01mm.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/d1d308c1df1041809d052cf3f917d0b3"
  },
  {
    "key": "512e0c24-cf4d-4154-9b4b-35b612d63862",
    "name": "Item 18",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "18",
    "categoryHeading1": "Proceq Concrete scanning",
    "categoryHeading2": "Concrete scanning",
    "category": "<p>Non-destructive testing of concrete structures using stepped frequency continuous-wave ground penetrating radar to an effective depth exceeding 700mm.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/1d19ea6aa8c64ae68b01095183eaca02"
  },
  {
    "key": "6943d597-e69e-4e8d-b6f3-0abb39886a69",
    "name": "Item 19",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "19",
    "categoryHeading1": "Certification of a binder distributor ",
    "categoryHeading2": "a binder distributor ",
    "category": "<p>These tests are conducted for the fit-for-purpose certification of a binder distributor. Tests are conducted annually and include the certification of a binder distributor, validation of binder distributor dipstick, power and speed indicator test, pump system performance and transverse distribution.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/f729aeba0fdd44f4b9ca299ca5552b11"
  },
  {
    "key": "1c0675f9-5cf9-4cae-b107-fe9248d2302d",
    "name": "Item 20",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "20",
    "categoryHeading1": "Marvil test",
    "categoryHeading2": "test",
    "category": "<p>This test is used to determine the in-situ water permeability of bituminous surfacing. The permeability of the bituminous layer provides an indication of the interconnectivity of the voids in the layer. The results provide an indication of the material’s susceptibility to the ingress of water.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/0d99d5c7def3405f92d6b32658447a56"
  },
  {
    "key": "dcd81f90-dd8b-46b9-bb70-1e05a6987f68",
    "name": "Item 21",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "21",
    "categoryHeading1": "Texture depth measurement ",
    "categoryHeading2": "depth measurement ",
    "category": "<p>This test is used to determine the texture of a road surface (the roughness).</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/a478384949484bc7a94b555c7222ac3d"
  },
  {
    "key": "5b04b451-77a5-4eb3-becf-19e75034e7f8",
    "name": "Item 22",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "22",
    "categoryHeading1": "Ball penetration ",
    "categoryHeading2": "penetration ",
    "category": "<p>The ball penetration test is used to simulate the embedment of stone chips that occurs during construction and under traffic loading.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/8376eb066e3e409aa20972582c6ec243"
  },
  {
    "key": "71d62bc2-bc70-4504-9bf5-024a3d4f5718",
    "name": "Item 23",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "23",
    "categoryHeading1": "Cover meter testing ",
    "categoryHeading2": "testing ",
    "category": "<p>Determining the cover to embedded reinforcing in an existing concrete structure with the use of a rebar detector/cover meter.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/470c61ae6c554ff89c4ae9df1cc96899"
  },
  {
    "key": "62545ae1-1702-440c-9fb1-26704051142e",
    "name": "Item 24",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "24",
    "categoryHeading1": "Rebound hammer ",
    "categoryHeading2": "hammer ",
    "category": "<p>A Schmidt hammer, also known as a Rebound hammer or Concrete hammer test, is a device to measure the elastic properties or strength of concrete or rock, mainly surface hardness and penetration resistance.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/0121d57ab47b4f088186178238d08b00"
  },
  {
    "key": "3c014c76-5239-46ce-a3b5-446133af111c",
    "name": "Item 25",
    "ncContentTypeAlias": "products",
    "categoryNumber": "25",
    "categoryHeading1": "Ultrasonic pulse velocity meter (UPV)",
    "categoryHeading2": "(UPV)",
    "category": "<p>Pulses of ultrasonic waves are transmitted into concrete structures to determine the uniformity of concrete, indicate voids, estimate the depth of surface voids and check on the effectiveness of crack repairs and severity of damage or deterioration of concrete.</p>",
    "categoryImage": "umb://media/bc50ba2dcda14e2f8fc67a3ca6e34ede"
  }
]]]></Value>
    </serviceCategories>
